course: dictionary
lesson: 13834
title: Jailer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jailer is a person whose job is to look after the prisoners in a jail and keep them locked in. Read the clues in the sentence: «The jailer turned the big iron key and locked the cell door.» Turned, key, cell and locked all show what a jailer does.
explain: Look at the word «gaoler» too. It is an older spelling, used in the UK, and it means exactly the same as jailer. In The Wind in the Willows, the gaoler's daughter feels sorry for Toad, who is locked in a dungeon, and she helps him escape.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try: «Every morning the jailer brought bread to the prisoners.» Does jailer still make sense there? If you think of a person who looks after prisoners, it does.
fact: A jailer is a person who looks after prisoners and keeps them locked in.
fact: «Jailer» and «gaoler» are two spellings of the same word; «gaoler» is the older UK spelling.
fact: Jailers often hold the keys, bring food and guard the cells.
fact: Today the job is often called «prison officer», or «correctional officer» in the USA.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the gaoler's daughter helps Toad escape by dressing him as a washerwoman.
exercise: «The jailer turned the big iron key and locked the cell door.» What is a jailer? | A person who sells keys in a shop | A guard who protects a bank | *A person who looks after prisoners and keeps them locked in | A prisoner who has been set free
exercise: Oliver says a jailer is a teacher who marks spelling tests. Is he right? | *No, but a teacher works in a school, and a jailer works in a jail | No, a jailer looks after prisoners in a jail | Yes, because both jobs are at school | Yes, because both jobs use a lot of keys
exercise: «The jailer kept the thief locked in the cell all night.» Find and copy one word that means shut in safely. | *locked | thief | cell | night
test: «The gaoler's daughter helped Toad escape.» Gaoler is an older spelling of which word? | Lawyer | *Jailer | Soldier | Judge
test: Today the job of a jailer in the UK is often called what? | Teacher | *Prison officer | Gardener | Pilot
exam: «The jailer heard a noise in the night and checked every cell.» Which job is most like a jailer's? | *Prison officer who guards prisoners and checks their cells | Gardener who waters the flowers | Driver who takes people to the shops | Baker who bakes bread for the shops
